---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import lespaulImage from '../assets/images/now/guitars/les paul.jpg';
import stratImage from '../assets/images/now/guitars/strat.jpg';
import embassyImage from '../assets/images/now/guitars/embassy.jpg';
import morrisImage from '../assets/images/now/guitars/morris.jpg';

const pageTitle = "Guitars - Thamara Kandabada";
---
<PageLayout title={pageTitle}>
    <h1>Guitars</h1>
    <p>This page is dedicated to guitars: those I currently own, want to own, and am interested in for any reason.</p>
    <p>A majority of the music I consume is guitar-based, and I play guitar at a beginner level. I keep buying guitars hoping that skill will follow. (It hasn’t happened yet.) Fortunately for you, the music I make is not available for public consumption.</p>
    <p>I've written about how and why I started playing guitar <a href="/notebook/2026/08/guitaring">here</a>.</p>
    <h2>My current collection</h2>
      <div class="guitar-showcase">
      <div class="guitar">
        <h3>Epiphone 1959 Les Paul Standard</h3>
        <figure>
              <Picture
                src={lespaulImage}
                alt="Epiphone Les Paul Standard electric guitar with Mahogany body finished in Aged Gloss and Laurel fretboard"
                formats={['avif', 'webp']}
              />
        </figure>
        <p><strong>Body material and finish:</strong> Mahogany, Aged Gloss</p>
        <p><strong>Fretboard:</strong> Laurel</p>
        <p><strong>Purchase date:</strong> 14 November 2023</p>
        <p><strong>Purchase price:</strong> £749</p>
        <p>This guitar is full of character. I love the raw energy of the sound, and even though it goes out of tune faster than you can say "Les Paul" it's a joy to play. It's the kind of machine you feel powerful just holding.</p>
        <p><a href="https://www.gibson.com/en-gb/products/epiphone-1959-les-paul-standard-incl-hard-case-aged-dark-burst" target="_blank">View full spec</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="guitar">
        <h3>Fender Player Series Stratocaster</h3>
        <figure>
              <Picture
                src={stratImage}
                alt="Fender Player Stratocaster electric guitar with Alder body finished in Tidepool and Maple fretboard"
                formats={['avif', 'webp']}
              />
        </figure>
        <p><strong>Body material and finish:</strong> Alder, Tidepool</p>
        <p><strong>Fretboard:</strong> Maple</p>
        <p><strong>Purchase date:</strong> 3 January 2023</p>
        <p><strong>Purchase price:</strong> £499</p>
        <p>This Strat produces the clean Fender tone that you'd expect from it and feels great to play. It works well with my small but dependable Fender Champion 20 amplifier.</p>
        <p><a href="https://www.promusicalaska.com/store/guitars/electric-guitars/fender-player-stratocaster-tidepool-maple-fingerboard/?print=pdf" target="_blank">View full spec</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="guitar">
        <h3>Epiphone Embassy (Bass)</h3>
        <figure>
              <Picture
                src={embassyImage}
                alt="Epiphone Embassy electric bass guitar with Mahogany body finished in Graphite Black body and Laurel fretboard"
                formats={['avif', 'webp']}
              />
        </figure>
        <p><strong>Body material and finish:</strong> Mahogany, Graphite Black</p>
        <p><strong>Fretboard:</strong> Laurel</p>
        <p><strong>Purchase date:</strong> 22 March 2023</p>
        <p><strong>Purchase price:</strong> £349</p>
        <p>Although this is my lease picked up guitar, I like having the option in my collection. I like plugging in my compact bass headphone amplifier directly to this for some good old fashion grooving for an audience of one.</p>
        <p><a href="https://www.gibson.com/en-gb/products/epiphone-embassy-bass-graphite-black" target="_blank">View full spec</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="guitar">
        <h3>Morris W-18</h3>
        <figure>
              <Picture
                src={morrisImage}
                alt="Morris W-18 acoustic dreadnought guitar with Spruce and Mahogany body in natural finish and Rosewood fretboard"
                formats={['avif', 'webp']}
              />
        </figure>
        <p><strong>Body material and finish:</strong> Spruce & Mahogany, Natural</p>
        <p><strong>Fretboard:</strong> Rosewood</p>
        <p><strong>Purchase date:</strong> c. 2021</p>
        <p><strong>Purchase price:</strong> £0</p>
        <p>The best guitar is a free guitar. Although I had to spend some money fixing the completely twisted out of shape neck on this guitar, I still think of it as a freebie. It has a nice, rich sound.</p>
        <p><a href="https://www.coololdguitars.shop/products/1980s-morris-w-18-japanese-vintage-acoustic-dreadnought-guitar-natural" target="_blank">View full spec</a></p>
      </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Amps</h2>
      <h2>Interfaces</h2>
      <h2>Wishlist</h2>
</PageLayout>